# Credentials — NEVER commit. Copy .env.example to .env and fill in.
.env
*.pem

# Customer evidence (filenames contain customer names) and browser profiles
# (contain logged-in sessions/cookies).
ScreenShot*/
screen_shot/
user_data/
# assets/ is a runtime cache (pimeyes _remote_cache), created on demand.
assets/

# NOTE: sites_scan_google/ is NOT ignored — despite the name it is source,
# not output: __scanGoogle.py imports sites_scan_google.<domain> at runtime.
# Same trap that lib/ fell into. Do not add it here.

# Virtualenv.
#
# On Windows the venv lives in the pipeline root itself, and the filesystem is
# case-insensitive — so `Lib\` (venv) and `lib\` (our 8 custom modules) are the
# SAME directory. That is why only `site-packages` is excluded here and never
# `lib/` or `Lib/` wholesale: ignoring the directory would drop
# broker_helpers.py, automation_delay.py, captcha.py, common.py,
# email_sender.py, email_verification.py, proxies.py and safe_browser.py from
# the repo, and manage.py will not start without them.
Lib/site-packages/
lib/site-packages/
Include/
Scripts/
pyvenv.cfg

# On this Linux copy the whole venv sits under removal/ (Scripts, lib,
# pyvenv.cfg). The 8 custom modules are now kept at the top-level lib/ —
# the path manage.py actually imports and the path the VPS uses — so
# excluding the venv folder no longer drops them.
removal/

# Belt and braces: the custom modules are tracked no matter what.
!lib/*.py
!Lib/*.py

# NOTE: adblock/ IS tracked (378MB, 745 files). It is committed so a rebuilt
# server gets the ad blocker straight from the clone. manage.py still patches
# add_extension to skip a missing folder, so a shallow/partial checkout works.

# Runtime state and junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
logs/
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
dump.rdb
*.rdb
ccpa_email_counter.json
captcha.png
__downloaded.mp3
info.jpeg
extension.zip
pkgs.txt
